        <mxCell id="XDFivQQymPn6_W2-JGWK-64" parent="1" style="verticalAlign=top;align=left;overflow=fill;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Officers possessed the correct warrant information but failed to verify the residence&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center; margin: 4px 0px 0px; text-decoration-color: currentcolor;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Hartsfield v. Lemacks&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;&#x9;&quot;Newton had the warrant in his possession, he did not check to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;make sure that he was leading the other officers to the correct address,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;let alone perform any precautionary measures such as those performed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;by the officers in Garrison. . . . the district court erred in holding that he w&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0px;margin-left:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;as protected by qualified immunity&quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt;Hartsfield v. Lemacks, 50 F.3d 950, 955 (11th Cir. 1995), as amended (June 14, 1995)&#x9;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
